<title>UK: Vanguard Medica up on SmithKline deal.</title>
<headline>Vanguard Medica up on SmithKline deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British drug research group Vanguard Medica Group Plc rose on Monday after news that drug giant SmithKline Beecham Plc would take up the company's worldwide marketing of its migraine drug, VML 251.</p>
<p>Vanguard's shares rose 57-1/2p at 567-1/2p by 0834 GMT with over 3,000 shares changing hands.</p>
<p>The company said the results of clinical studies of VML 251 were most encouraging and showed that a distinctive profile was emerging for the new drug.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom ++ 44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
